ads to an asymmetric superposition. A detuning ∆′ ≃ √ Nχ helps balance the phase diffusion rate between the particles, leading to roughly symmetric superpositions."}]}, {"reference": {"label": "34", "publication_info": {"journal_volume": "62", "artid": "013607", "year": 2000, "journal_title": "Phys.Rev.A"}, "authors": [{"full_name": "Dalvit, D.A.R."}, {"full_name": "Dziarmaga, J."}, {"full_name": "Zurek, W.H."}]}, "raw_refs": [{"schema": "text", "source": "arXiv", "value": "[34] D. A. R. Dalvit, J. Dziarmaga, and W. H. Zurek, Phys. Rev. A 62, 013607 (2000)."}]}], "number_of_pages": 4, "referenced_authors_bais": ["S.Haroche.1", "Jonathan.R.Friedman.1", "D.F.Walls.1", "R.Graham.1", "M.J.Collett.1", "J.Ruostekoski.2", "R.Kowalski.1", "D.J.Wineland.1", "S.K.Tolpygo.1", "V.Patel.3", "A.Garg.4", "D.M.Meekhof.1", "L.M.Duan.1", "O.Nairz.1", "J.I.Cirac.1", "K.Goral.1", "J.M.Raimond.1", "P.Zoller.1", "M.Kostrun.1", "G.van.der.Zouw.1", "F.Laloe.1", "M.Brune.1", "B.Yurke.1", "K.Moelmer.1", "A.J.Leggett.1", "E.Hagley.1", "W.Chen.53", "J.E.Lukens.1", "B.E.King.1", "X.Maitre.1", "C.Wunderlich.2", "A.Maali.1", "M.Mackie.1", "M.Arndt.1", "K.Rzazewski.1", "J.VosAndreae.1", "J.Javanainen.3", "D.Stoler.1", "A.S.Sorensen.1", "E.Schrodinger.1", "R.E.Cote.2", "C.Monroe.2", "A.Zeilinger.1", "M.Lewenstein.1", "M.Gajda.1", "J.Dreyer.1", "C.Keller.1"], "inspire_categories": [{"term": "Condensed Matter", "source": "arxiv"}, {"term": "General Physics", "source": "arxiv"}, {"term": "Other", "source": "arxiv"}, {"term": "Quantum Physics", "source": "arxiv"}], "figures": [{"filename": "figure1.png", "material": "preprint", "caption": "Three-level illustration of coherent free-bound- bound photoassociation, where $N$ atoms have assumedly Bose-condensed into state $|1\\rangle$. The free-bound and bound- bound Rabi frequencies are $\\kappa$ and $\\Omega$, respectively. Similarly, the two-photon and intermediate detunings are $\\Delta$ and $\\delta$. The wavy line denotes the irreversible losses that a large $|\\delta|$ is expected to combat.", "source": "arxiv", "label": "THREEL", "key": "800e8f6f86b1f966b6f4520753818311", "url": "https://inspirehep.net/files/800e8f6f86b1f966b6f4520753818311"}, {"filename": "figure2.png", "material": "preprint", "caption": "Creation of a macroscopic superposition of atoms and molecules by photoassociating a BEC of atoms. The frequency scale is defined by $\\lambda=1$, the dimensionless time is $\\tau=\\sqrt{N}\\chi (t-\\bar{t})$, and the initial state is $|\\psi_i\\rangle=|N,0\\rangle$ with $N=5000$ atoms and $n=0$ molecules. (a) For $\\varphi=\\pi/2$, a strong and two-photon resonant photoassociation pulse forms a symmetric joint atom-molecule condensate with a real amplitude: $|\\psi(\\tau=0)\\rangle=\\sum_{n=0}^{N/2} C_n(0)|N-2n,n\\rangle$, Im$[C_n(0)]=0$. Switching to $[\\varphi,\\chi,\\Delta']=[0,0.1\\sqrt{N},0.1N\\,]$, the system evolves (b) into a coherent superposition of atoms and molecules and (c) back to a symmetric atom-molecule condensate.", "source": "arxiv", "label": "FATCAT", "key": "a3ec52bde0918c5420be9a1015764fab", "url": "https://inspirehep.net/files/a3ec52bde0918c5420be9a1015764fab"}], "preprint_date": "2001-08-17", "author_count": 3, "first_author": {"full_name": "Calsamiglia, John", "last_name": "Calsamiglia", "first_name": "John", "recid": 1992720}, "public_notes": [{"source": "arXiv", "value": "4 pages, 2 figs, to appear in Phys. Rev. Lett"}], "control_number": 2987986, "dois": [{"material": "publication", "source": "arXiv", "value": "10.1103/PhysRevLett.87.160403"}], "earliest_date": "2001-08-17", "document_type": ["article"], "texkeys": ["Calsamiglia:2001oum"], "abstracts": [{"source": "arXiv", "value": "We theoretically examine photoassociation of a non-ideal Bose-Einstein condensate, focusing on evidence for a macroscopic superposition of atoms and molecules. This problem raises an interest because, rather than two states of a given object, an atom-molecule system is a seemingly impossible macroscopic superposition of different objects. Nevertheless, photoassociation enables coherent intraparticle conversion, and we thereby propose a viable scheme for creating a superposition of a macroscopic number of atoms with a macroscopic number of molecules.", "abstract_source_suggest": {"input": "arXiv"}}], "primary_arxiv_category": ["cond-mat.soft"], "titles": [{"source": "arXiv", "title": "Superposition of macroscopic numbers of atoms and molecules"}], "facet_author_name": ["1992720_John Calsamiglia", "2215130_Kalle-Antti Suominen", "2567433_Matt Mackie"], "_oai": {"sets": ["Literature"], "id": "oai:inspirehep.net:2987986", "updated": "2026-02-09T15:02:17.046262"}, "curated": false, "journal_title_variants": ["Phys.Rev.Lett.", "Phys. Rev. Lett."], "arxiv_eprints": [{"categories": ["cond-mat.soft", "physics.atom-ph", "physics.chem-ph", "quant-ph"], "value": "cond-mat/0103437"}]}, "id": "2987986", "created": "2025-10-01T10:53:20.417558+00:00", "updated": "2026-02-09T15:02:17.046262+00:00"}], "total": 1}, "links": {"self": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=doi%3A10.1103%2Fphysrevlett.87.160403&size=5&page=1", "bibtex": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=doi%3A10.1103%2Fphysrevlett.87.160403&size=5&page=1&format=bibtex", "latex-eu": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=doi%3A10.1103%2Fphysrevlett.87.160403&size=5&page=1&format=latex-eu", "latex-us": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=doi%3A10.1103%2Fphysrevlett.87.160403&size=5&page=1&format=latex-us", "json": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=doi%3A10.1103%2Fphysrevlett.87.160403&size=5&page=1&format=json", "json-expanded": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=doi%3A10.1103%2Fphysrevlett.87.160403&size=5&page=1&format=json-expanded", "cv": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=doi%3A10.1103%2Fphysrevlett.87.160403&size=5&page=1&format=cv"}}